IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa24-prosecution.l4: Part 36, ss 1126 to 1130 and 1132 to 1133 of the Companies Act 2006: consents, venue, time limits,
-- privilege, unincorporated bodies, production of documents, financial penalties and the transitional provision
-- (lines 16092-16145 and 16149-16189 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE ANSWERS FOR THE OTHER PARTS. The plan's seam `s 1128 the information was laid in time` is answered by
-- `s 1128(1) the information was laid in time` (England and Wales), `s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in
-- time` and `s 1128(3) the complaint was made in time` (Northern Ireland).
--
-- WHAT IS NOT ENCODED. s 1124 (Schedule 3, amendments of the Companies Act 1985) is an amendment of another Act: machinery,
-- inert (reason 2). s 1132A(1), (3), (6), (7) are regulation-making powers and the payment of receipts into the Consolidated
-- Fund: machinery, inert (reason 2) in NOTES.md. ss 1125 and 1131 are in coa24-penalty.l4; ss 1121 to 1123 are in
-- coa24-officers.l4.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29; assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). MAYBE answers: JUST TRUE is the text
-- saying yes; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"`); NOTHING is "not covered" (each NOTHING branch says why,
-- as `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). The periods in s 1128 are fixed in the text's own words, so outside a period the answer is
-- JUST FALSE (the ruling of 2026-11-05, (a)). "three years after" and "twelve months after" are counted with daydate's
-- `add years` and `add months`, which clamp the day of the month (29 February plus three years is 28 February): fork F6.

§ `Part 36: consents, venue, time limits and production of documents (ss 1126 to 1133)`

-- ---- s 1126 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1126(1) offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 1126(1) an offence under section 458, 460 or 949 of this Act (unauthorised disclosure of information)`
    `s 1126(1) an offence under section 953 of this Act (failure to comply with rules about takeover bid documents)`
    `s 1126(1) an offence under section 448, 449, 450, 451 or 453A of the Companies Act 1985 (offences in connection with company investigations)`
    `s 1126(1) an offence under section 798 of this Act (attempting to evade restrictions on shares)`
    `s 1126(1) an offence under section 455 of the Companies Act 1985 (attempting to evade restrictions on shares)`
    `s 1126(1) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A of this Act (false statement offences)`
    `s 1126(1) an offence under paragraph 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to this Act (breach of certain restrictions imposed under that Schedule)`
    `s 1126(1) another offence`

DECLARE `s 1126 consent of` IS ONE OF
    `s 1126 the Secretary of State`
    `s 1126 the Director of Public Prosecutions`
    `s 1126 the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland`
    `s 1126 no one`

DECLARE `s 1126 consent required` IS ONE OF
    `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions`
    `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland`
    `s 1126 the Secretary of State alone`

-- src:16093 | (1) This section applies to proceedings for an offence under any of the following provisions—
-- src:16094 | section 458, 460 or 949 of this Act (offences of unauthorised disclosure of information);
-- src:16095 | section 953 of this Act (failure to comply with rules about takeover bid documents);
-- src:16096 | section 448, 449, 450, 451 or 453A of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) (offences in connection with company investigations);
-- src:16097 | section 798 of this Act or section 455 of the Companies Act 1985 (offence of attempting to evade restrictions on shares).
-- src:16098 | section 1112 or 1112A of this Act (false statement offences);
-- src:16099 | paragraph 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to this Act (breach of certain restrictions imposed under that Schedule)
-- src:16100 | (2) No such proceedings are to be brought in England and Wales except by or with the consent of—
-- src:16101 | (a) in the case of an offence under—
-- src:16102 | (i) section 458, 460 or 949 of this Act,
-- src:16103 | (ii) section 953 of this Act, ...
-- src:16104 | (iii) section 448, 449, 450, 451 or 453A of the Companies Act 1985, or
-- src:16105 | (iv) section 1112 or 1112A of this Act,
-- src:16106 | the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions;
-- src:16107 | (b) in the case of an offence under section 798 of , or paragraph 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to, this Act or section 455 of the Companies Act 1985, the Secretary of State.
-- src:16108 | (3) No such proceedings are to be brought in Northern Ireland except by or with the consent of—
-- src:16109 | (a) in the case of an offence under—
-- src:16110 | (i) section 458, 460 or 949 of this Act,
-- src:16111 | (ii) section 953 of this Act, ...
-- src:16112 | (iii) section 448, 449, 450, 451 or 453A of the Companies Act 1985, or
-- src:16113 | (iv) section 1112 or 1112A of this Act,
-- src:16114 | the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland;
-- src:16115 | (b) in the case of an offence under section 798 of , or paragraph 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to, this Act or section 455 of the Companies Act 1985, the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1126 Consents required for certain prosecutions (src:16093-16115)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 1126(1) offence`
      place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1126 consent required`
`s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN
        CONSIDER offence
        WHEN `s 1126(1) an offence under section 458, 460 or 949 of this Act (unauthorised disclosure of information)` THEN JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions`
        WHEN `s 1126(1) an offence under section 953 of this Act (failure to comply with rules about takeover bid documents)` THEN JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions`
        WHEN `s 1126(1) an offence under section 448, 449, 450, 451 or 453A of the Companies Act 1985 (offences in connection with company investigations)` THEN JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions`
        WHEN `s 1126(1) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A of this Act (false statement offences)` THEN JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions`
        WHEN `s 1126(1) an offence under section 798 of this Act (attempting to evade restrictions on shares)` THEN JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State alone`
        WHEN `s 1126(1) an offence under section 455 of the Companies Act 1985 (attempting to evade restrictions on shares)` THEN JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State alone`
        WHEN `s 1126(1) an offence under paragraph 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to this Act (breach of certain restrictions imposed under that Schedule)` THEN JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State alone`
        WHEN `s 1126(1) another offence` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section applies to proceedings for an offence under the listed provisions
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN
        CONSIDER offence
        WHEN `s 1126(1) an offence under section 458, 460 or 949 of this Act (unauthorised disclosure of information)` THEN JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland`
        WHEN `s 1126(1) an offence under section 953 of this Act (failure to comply with rules about takeover bid documents)` THEN JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland`
        WHEN `s 1126(1) an offence under section 448, 449, 450, 451 or 453A of the Companies Act 1985 (offences in connection with company investigations)` THEN JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland`
        WHEN `s 1126(1) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A of this Act (false statement offences)` THEN JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland`
        WHEN `s 1126(1) an offence under section 798 of this Act (attempting to evade restrictions on shares)` THEN JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State alone`
        WHEN `s 1126(1) an offence under section 455 of the Companies Act 1985 (attempting to evade restrictions on shares)` THEN JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State alone`
        WHEN `s 1126(1) an offence under paragraph 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to this Act (breach of certain restrictions imposed under that Schedule)` THEN JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State alone`
        WHEN `s 1126(1) another offence` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section applies to proceedings for an offence under the listed provisions
    WHEN Scotland THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsections (2) and (3) speak of England and Wales and Northern Ireland and say nothing of Scotland

-- "No such proceedings are to be brought ... except by or with the consent of": without the consent of a person named the
-- answer is JUST FALSE; with it the "except" is met and the section does not itself say the proceedings may be brought (NOTHING).
@ref s 1126(2)-(3) No such proceedings are to be brought except by or with the consent named (src:16100-16115)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 1126(1) offence`
      place IS A `Place of registration`
      `the proceedings are brought by, or with the consent of` IS A `s 1126 consent of`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1126(2)-(3) the proceedings may be brought` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` offence place
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence or place is not one for which subsection (2) or (3) requires a consent
    WHEN JUST required THEN
        CONSIDER required
        WHEN `s 1126 the Secretary of State alone` THEN
            IF `the proceedings are brought by, or with the consent of` EQUALS `s 1126 the Secretary of State`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the "except" is met; the section bars proceedings without the consent and does not itself say they may be brought
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No such proceedings are to be brought in England and Wales except by or with the consent of ... the Secretary of State"
        WHEN `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions` THEN
            IF `the proceedings are brought by, or with the consent of` EQUALS `s 1126 the Secretary of State` OR `the proceedings are brought by, or with the consent of` EQUALS `s 1126 the Director of Public Prosecutions`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the "except" is met; the section bars proceedings without the consent and does not itself say they may be brought
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No such proceedings are to be brought in England and Wales except by or with the consent of ... the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions"
        WHEN `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland` THEN
            IF `the proceedings are brought by, or with the consent of` EQUALS `s 1126 the Secretary of State` OR `the proceedings are brought by, or with the consent of` EQUALS `s 1126 the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the "except" is met; the section bars proceedings without the consent and does not itself say they may be brought
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No such proceedings are to be brought in Northern Ireland except by or with the consent of ... the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland"

-- ---- s 1127 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16117 | (1) Summary proceedings for any offence under the Companies Acts may be taken—
-- src:16118 | (a) against a body corporate, at any place at which the body has a place of business, and
-- src:16119 | (b) against any other person, at any place at which he is for the time being.
@ref s 1127(1) Summary proceedings may be taken against a body corporate where it has a place of business, against any other person where he is (src:16117-16119)
GIVEN `the defendant is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is a place at which the body has a place of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is a place at which the defendant is for the time being` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1127(1) summary proceedings for the offence may be taken at the place` MEANS
    IF `the defendant is a body corporate`
    THEN IF `the place is a place at which the body has a place of business`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against a body corporate, at any place at which the body has a place of business"; subsection (2) leaves any other jurisdiction untouched
    ELSE IF `the place is a place at which the defendant is for the time being`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against any other person, at any place at which he is for the time being"; subsection (2) leaves any other jurisdiction untouched

-- src:16120 | (2) This is without prejudice to any jurisdiction exercisable apart from this section.
@ref s 1127(2) Without prejudice to any jurisdiction exercisable apart from this section (src:16120)
GIVEN `a jurisdiction is exercisable apart from this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1127(2) section 1127(1) prejudices the jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `a jurisdiction is exercisable apart from this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is without prejudice to any jurisdiction exercisable apart from this section"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a jurisdiction exercisable apart from the section

-- ---- s 1128 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) England and Wales: "within three years after the commission of the offence" and "within twelve months after the date on
-- which evidence sufficient ... comes to his knowledge". The date the evidence came to the knowledge of the Director of Public
-- Prosecutions or the Secretary of State is the judgment of someone else: an input, MAYBE DATE (see also (4)).
-- src:16122 | (1) An information relating to an offence under the Companies Acts that is triable by a magistrates' court in England and Wales may be so tried if it is laid—
-- src:16123 | (a) at any time within three years after the commission of the offence, and
-- src:16124 | (b) within twelve months after the date on which evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State (as the case may be) to justify the proceedings comes to his knowledge.
@ref s 1128(1) England and Wales: the information must be laid within three years and twelve months (src:16122-16124)
GIVEN `date the offence was committed` IS A DATE
      `date the information was laid` IS A DATE
      `date on which evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1128(1) the information was laid in time` MEANS
    IF `date the information was laid` GREATER THAN (`add years` `date the offence was committed` 3)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is laid— (a) at any time within three years after the commission of the offence"
    ELSE CONSIDER `date on which evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge`
         WHEN JUST knowledge THEN
             IF `date the information was laid` AT MOST (`add months` knowledge 12)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) within twelve months after the date on which evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State (as the case may be) to justify the proceedings comes to his knowledge"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the date on which the evidence came to the knowledge of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State is for them and was not supplied

-- (2) Scotland.
-- src:16125 | (2) Summary proceedings in Scotland for an offence under the Companies Acts—
-- src:16126 | (a) must not be commenced after the expiration of three years from the commission of the offence;
-- src:16127 | (b) subject to that, may be commenced at any time—
-- src:16128 | (i) within twelve months after the date on which evidence sufficient in the Lord Advocate's opinion to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge, or
-- src:16129 | (ii) where such evidence was reported to him by the Secretary of State, within twelve months after the date on which it came to the knowledge of the latter.
-- src:16130 | Section 136(3) of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995 (c. 46) (date when proceedings deemed to be commenced) applies for the purposes of this subsection as for the purposes of that section.
@ref s 1128(2) Scotland: proceedings must not be commenced after three years, and within twelve months of the knowledge (src:16125-16130)
GIVEN `date the offence was committed` IS A DATE
      `date the proceedings are deemed to be commenced (section 136(3) of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995)` IS A DATE
      `date on which evidence sufficient in the Lord Advocate's opinion to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the evidence was reported to the Lord Advocate by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date on which the evidence came to the knowledge of the Secretary of State` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in time` MEANS
    IF `date the proceedings are deemed to be commenced (section 136(3) of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995)` GREATER THAN (`add years` `date the offence was committed` 3)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be commenced after the expiration of three years from the commission of the offence"
    ELSE CONSIDER `date on which evidence sufficient in the Lord Advocate's opinion to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge`
         WHEN JUST laKnowledge THEN
             IF `date the proceedings are deemed to be commenced (section 136(3) of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995)` AT MOST (`add months` laKnowledge 12)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE IF `the evidence was reported to the Lord Advocate by the Secretary of State`
                  THEN CONSIDER `date on which the evidence came to the knowledge of the Secretary of State`
                       WHEN JUST sosKnowledge THEN
                           IF `date the proceedings are deemed to be commenced (section 136(3) of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995)` AT MOST (`add months` sosKnowledge 12)
                           THEN JUST TRUE
                           ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be commenced at any time— (i) within twelve months after the date on which evidence sufficient in the Lord Advocate's opinion to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge, or (ii) where such evidence was reported to him by the Secretary of State, within twelve months after the date on which it came to the knowledge of the latter"
                       WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the date on which the evidence came to the knowledge of the Secretary of State was not supplied
                  ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) subject to that, may be commenced at any time— (i) within twelve months after the date on which evidence sufficient in the Lord Advocate's opinion to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             IF `the evidence was reported to the Lord Advocate by the Secretary of State`
             THEN CONSIDER `date on which the evidence came to the knowledge of the Secretary of State`
                  WHEN JUST sosKnowledge THEN
                      IF `date the proceedings are deemed to be commenced (section 136(3) of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995)` AT MOST (`add months` sosKnowledge 12)
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the date on which the evidence came to the knowledge of the Lord Advocate is for him and was not supplied
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the dates on which the evidence came to the knowledge of the Lord Advocate and of the Secretary of State were not supplied
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the date on which the evidence came to the knowledge of the Lord Advocate is for him and was not supplied

-- (3) Northern Ireland.
-- src:16131 | (3) A magistrates' court in Northern Ireland has jurisdiction to hear and determine a complaint charging the commission of a summary offence under the Companies Acts provided that the complaint is made—
-- src:16132 | (a) within three years from the time when the offence was committed, and
-- src:16133 | (b) within twelve months from the date on which evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State (as the case may be) to justify the proceedings comes to his knowledge.
@ref s 1128(3) Northern Ireland: the complaint must be made within three years and twelve months (src:16131-16133)
GIVEN `date the offence was committed` IS A DATE
      `date the complaint was made` IS A DATE
      `date on which evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1128(3) the complaint was made in time` MEANS
    IF `date the complaint was made` GREATER THAN (`add years` `date the offence was committed` 3)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that the complaint is made— (a) within three years from the time when the offence was committed"
    ELSE CONSIDER `date on which evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge`
         WHEN JUST knowledge THEN
             IF `date the complaint was made` AT MOST (`add months` knowledge 12)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) within twelve months from the date on which evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State (as the case may be) to justify the proceedings comes to his knowledge"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the date on which the evidence came to the knowledge of the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State is for them and was not supplied

-- (4) A certificate is conclusive evidence of the date: it supplies the date that (1) to (3) take as an input.
-- src:16134 | (4) For the purposes of this section a certificate of the Director of Public Prosecutions, the Lord Advocate, the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State (as the case may be) as to the date on which such evidence as is referred to above came to his notice is conclusive evidence.
@ref s 1128(4) A certificate is conclusive evidence of the date on which the evidence came to notice (src:16134)
GIVEN `the date stated in a certificate of the Director of Public Prosecutions, the Lord Advocate, the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 1128(4) the date on which the evidence came to notice, as the certificate conclusively shows` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date stated in a certificate of the Director of Public Prosecutions, the Lord Advocate, the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State`
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a certificate

-- ---- s 1129 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16136 | In proceedings against a person for an offence under the Companies Acts, nothing in those Acts is to be taken to require any person to disclose any information that he is entitled to refuse to disclose on grounds of legal professional privilege (in Scotland, confidentiality of communications).
@ref s 1129 Legal professional privilege (src:16136)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings against a person for an offence under the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to refuse to disclose the information on grounds of legal professional privilege (in Scotland, confidentiality of communications)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1129 the Companies Acts require the person to disclose the information` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings against a person for an offence under the Companies Acts` AND `the person is entitled to refuse to disclose the information on grounds of legal professional privilege (in Scotland, confidentiality of communications)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In proceedings against a person for an offence under the Companies Acts, nothing in those Acts is to be taken to require any person to disclose any information that he is entitled to refuse to disclose on grounds of legal professional privilege"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section speaks only of proceedings for an offence under the Companies Acts and information the person may refuse to disclose on those grounds

-- ---- s 1130 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1130(1) name in which the proceedings are brought` IS ONE OF
    `s 1130(1) the name of the body`
    `s 1130(1) the name of a member of the body`

-- src:16138 | (1) Proceedings for an offence under the Companies Acts alleged to have been committed by an unincorporated body must be brought in the name of the body (and not in that of any of its members).
@ref s 1130(1) Proceedings against an unincorporated body must be brought in the name of the body (src:16138)
GIVEN `the proceedings are for an offence under the Companies Acts alleged to have been committed by an unincorporated body` IS A BOOLEAN
      name IS A `s 1130(1) name in which the proceedings are brought`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1130(1) the proceedings meet the requirement of s 1130(1)` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the proceedings are for an offence under the Companies Acts alleged to have been committed by an unincorporated body`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Proceedings for an offence under the Companies Acts alleged to have been committed by an unincorporated body"
    ELSE CONSIDER name
         WHEN `s 1130(1) the name of the body` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 1130(1) the name of a member of the body` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be brought in the name of the body (and not in that of any of its members)"

-- src:16139 | (2) For the purposes of such proceedings—
-- src:16140 | (a) any rules of court relating to the service of documents have effect as if the body were a body corporate, and
-- src:16141 | (b) the following provisions apply as they apply in relation to a body corporate—
-- src:16142 | (i) in England and Wales, section 33 of the Criminal Justice Act 1925 (c. 86) and Schedule 3 to the Magistrates' Courts Act 1980 (c. 43),
-- src:16143 | (ii) in Scotland, sections 70 and 143 of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995 (c. 46),
-- src:16144 | (iii) in Northern Ireland, section 18 of the Criminal Justice Act (Northern Ireland) 1945 (c. 15 (N.I.)) and Article 166 of and Schedule 4 to the Magistrates' Courts (Northern Ireland) Order 1981 (S.I. 1981/1675 (N.I. 26)).
@ref s 1130(2) For the proceedings the service rules and the listed provisions apply as for a body corporate (src:16139-16144)
GIVEN `the proceedings are for an offence under the Companies Acts alleged to have been committed by an unincorporated body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1130(2) the rules of court as to service, and the listed provisions, apply as if the body were a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are for an offence under the Companies Acts alleged to have been committed by an unincorporated body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of such proceedings"

@ref s 1130(2)(b) The provisions that apply as they apply in relation to a body corporate (src:16141-16144)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 1130(2)(b) the provisions that apply as they apply in relation to a body corporate` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN LIST
        "section 33 of the Criminal Justice Act 1925"
        "Schedule 3 to the Magistrates' Courts Act 1980"
    WHEN Scotland THEN LIST
        "section 70 of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995"
        "section 143 of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995"
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN LIST
        "section 18 of the Criminal Justice Act (Northern Ireland) 1945"
        "Article 166 of the Magistrates' Courts (Northern Ireland) Order 1981"
        "Schedule 4 to the Magistrates' Courts (Northern Ireland) Order 1981"

DECLARE `s 1130(3) funds out of which the fine is paid` IS ONE OF
    `s 1130(3) the funds of the body`
    `s 1130(3) the personal funds of a member of the body`

-- src:16145 | (3) A fine imposed on an unincorporated body on its conviction of an offence under the Companies Acts must be paid out of the funds of the body.
@ref s 1130(3) A fine imposed on an unincorporated body must be paid out of the funds of the body (src:16145)
GIVEN `a fine is imposed on an unincorporated body on its conviction of an offence under the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
      funds IS A `s 1130(3) funds out of which the fine is paid`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1130(3) the fine is paid as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a fine is imposed on an unincorporated body on its conviction of an offence under the Companies Acts`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A fine imposed on an unincorporated body on its conviction of an offence under the Companies Acts"
    ELSE CONSIDER funds
         WHEN `s 1130(3) the funds of the body` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 1130(3) the personal funds of a member of the body` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be paid out of the funds of the body"

-- ---- s 1132 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1132(1) applicant` IS ONE OF
    `s 1132(1)(a) the Director of Public Prosecutions (England and Wales)`
    `s 1132(1)(a) the Secretary of State (England and Wales)`
    `s 1132(1)(a) a chief officer of police (England and Wales)`
    `s 1132(1)(b) the Lord Advocate (Scotland)`
    `s 1132(1)(c) the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland`
    `s 1132(1)(c) the Department of Enterprise, Trade and Investment (Northern Ireland)`
    `s 1132(1)(c) a chief superintendent of the Police Service of Northern Ireland`
    `s 1132(1) some other person`

-- src:16151 | (1) An application under this section may be made—
-- src:16152 | (a) in England and Wales, to a judge of the High Court by the Director of Public Prosecutions, the Secretary of State or a chief officer of police;
-- src:16153 | (b) in Scotland, to one of the Lords Commissioners of Justiciary by the Lord Advocate;
-- src:16154 | (c) in Northern Ireland, to the High Court by the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland, the Department of Enterprise, Trade and Investment or a chief superintendent of the Police Service of Northern Ireland.
@ref s 1132(1) Who may apply, and to whom (src:16151-16154)
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 1132(1) applicant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1132(1) the person may apply for an order under this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER applicant
    WHEN `s 1132(1)(a) the Director of Public Prosecutions (England and Wales)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1132(1)(a) the Secretary of State (England and Wales)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1132(1)(a) a chief officer of police (England and Wales)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1132(1)(b) the Lord Advocate (Scotland)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1132(1)(c) the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1132(1)(c) the Department of Enterprise, Trade and Investment (Northern Ireland)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1132(1)(c) a chief superintendent of the Police Service of Northern Ireland` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1132(1) some other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application under this section may be made— (a) in England and Wales ... by the Director of Public Prosecutions, the Secretary of State or a chief officer of police" and so on, and the text does not say no one else may

@ref s 1132(1) The court to which the application is made (src:16152-16154)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 1132(1) the court to which the application is made` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN "a judge of the High Court"
    WHEN Scotland THEN "one of the Lords Commissioners of Justiciary"
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN "the High Court"

-- src:16155 | (2) If on an application under this section there is shown to be reasonable cause to believe—
-- src:16156 | (a) that any person has, while an officer of a company, committed an offence in connection with the management of the company's affairs, and
-- src:16157 | (b) that evidence of the commission of the offence is to be found in any documents in the possession or control of the company,
-- src:16158 | an order under this section may be made.
@ref s 1132(2) An order may be made where there is reasonable cause to believe an offence has been committed and evidence is in the company's documents (src:16155-16158)
GIVEN `there is shown to be reasonable cause to believe that a person has, while an officer of a company, committed an offence in connection with the management of the company's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is shown to be reasonable cause to believe that evidence of the commission of the offence is to be found in documents in the possession or control of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1132(2) an order under this section may be made` MEANS
    IF `there is shown to be reasonable cause to believe that a person has, while an officer of a company, committed an offence in connection with the management of the company's affairs` AND `there is shown to be reasonable cause to believe that evidence of the commission of the offence is to be found in documents in the possession or control of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If on an application under this section there is shown to be reasonable cause to believe— (a) that any person has, while an officer of a company, committed an offence in connection with the management of the company's affairs, and (b) that evidence of the commission of the offence is to be found in any documents in the possession or control of the company, an order under this section may be made"

DECLARE `s 1132(3) provision of the order` IS ONE OF
    `s 1132(3)(a) authority for a person named in the order to inspect the documents in question, or any of them, for the purpose of investigating and obtaining evidence of the offence`
    `s 1132(3)(b) a requirement that the secretary of the company, or such other officer of it as may be named in the order, produce the documents (or any of them) to a person named in the order at a place so named`

-- src:16159 | (3) The order may—
-- src:16160 | (a) authorise any person named in it to inspect the documents in question, or any of them, for the purpose of investigating and obtaining evidence of the offence, or
-- src:16161 | (b) require the secretary of the company, or such other officer of it as may be named in the order, to produce the documents (or any of them) to a person named in the order at a place so named.
-- src:16162 | (4) This section applies also in relation to documents in the possession or control of a person carrying on the business of banking, so far as they relate to the company's affairs, as it applies to documents in the possession or control of the company, except that no such order as is referred to in subsection (3)(b) may be made by virtue of this subsection.
@ref s 1132(3)-(4) What the order may contain, and the documents of a banker (src:16159-16162)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 1132(3) provision of the order`
      `an order under this section is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents are in the possession or control of a person carrying on the business of banking (so far as they relate to the company's affairs)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1132(3)-(4) the order may contain the provision` MEANS
    IF (NOT `an order under this section is made`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The order may"
    ELSE CONSIDER provision
         WHEN `s 1132(3)(a) authority for a person named in the order to inspect the documents in question, or any of them, for the purpose of investigating and obtaining evidence of the offence` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 1132(3)(b) a requirement that the secretary of the company, or such other officer of it as may be named in the order, produce the documents (or any of them) to a person named in the order at a place so named` THEN
             IF `the documents are in the possession or control of a person carrying on the business of banking (so far as they relate to the company's affairs)`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that no such order as is referred to in subsection (3)(b) may be made by virtue of this subsection"
             ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:16163 | (5) The decision under this section of a judge of the High Court, any of the Lords Commissioners of Justiciary or the High Court is not appealable.
@ref s 1132(5) The decision is not appealable (src:16163)
GIVEN `the decision is a decision under this section of a judge of the High Court, any of the Lords Commissioners of Justiciary or the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1132(5) the decision may be appealed` MEANS
    IF `the decision is a decision under this section of a judge of the High Court, any of the Lords Commissioners of Justiciary or the High Court`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The decision under this section of a judge of the High Court, any of the Lords Commissioners of Justiciary or the High Court is not appealable"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a decision under this section

-- src:16164 | (6) In this section “document” includes information recorded in any form.
@ref s 1132(6) "document" (src:16164)
GIVEN `the thing is information recorded in any form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1132(6) the thing is a document` MEANS
    IF `the thing is information recorded in any form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "In this section “document” includes information recorded in any form"

-- ---- s 1132A ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1132A(2) place of the offence provision in the Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 1132A(2)(a) Part 12 (company secretaries)`
    `s 1132A(2)(b) Part 13 (resolutions and meetings)`
    `s 1132A(2)(c) Part 16 (audit)`
    `s 1132A(2) some other provision of this Act`
    `s 1132A(2) a provision of another Act`

-- src:16168 | (2) “Relevant offence under this Act” means any offence under this Act other than an offence under a provision contained in—
-- src:16169 | (a) Part 12 (company secretaries);
-- src:16170 | (b) Part 13 (resolutions and meetings);
-- src:16171 | (c) Part 16 (audit).
@ref s 1132A(2) "Relevant offence under this Act" (src:16168-16171)
GIVEN place IS A `s 1132A(2) place of the offence provision in the Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1132A(2) the offence is a relevant offence under this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `s 1132A(2)(a) Part 12 (company secretaries)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Relevant offence under this Act” means any offence under this Act other than an offence under a provision contained in— (a) Part 12 (company secretaries)"
    WHEN `s 1132A(2)(b) Part 13 (resolutions and meetings)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than an offence under a provision contained in— ... (b) Part 13 (resolutions and meetings)"
    WHEN `s 1132A(2)(c) Part 16 (audit)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than an offence under a provision contained in— ... (c) Part 16 (audit)"
    WHEN `s 1132A(2) some other provision of this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1132A(2) a provision of another Act` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Relevant offence under this Act” means any offence under this Act"

-- (4): the regulations must ensure the maximum financial penalty does not exceed £10,000: above that is the text's no.
-- src:16178 | (4) Provision made under subsection (3)(b) must ensure that the maximum financial penalty that may be imposed does not exceed £10,000.
@ref s 1132A(4) The maximum financial penalty may not exceed 10,000 pounds (src:16178)
GIVEN `maximum financial penalty the regulations would allow, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1132A(4) the regulations may provide for this maximum financial penalty` MEANS
    IF `maximum financial penalty the regulations would allow, in pounds` GREATER THAN 10000
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Provision made under subsection (3)(b) must ensure that the maximum financial penalty that may be imposed does not exceed £10,000"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection caps the maximum at £10,000 and does not itself grant the power, which is in subsection (3)(b)

-- src:16179 | (5) The regulations must provide that—
-- src:16180 | (a) no financial penalty may be imposed under the regulations on a person in respect of conduct amounting to an offence if—
-- src:16181 | (i) proceedings have been brought against the person for that offence in respect of that conduct and the proceedings are ongoing, or
-- src:16182 | (ii) the person has been convicted of that offence in respect of that conduct, and
-- src:16183 | (b) no proceedings may be brought against a person in respect of conduct amounting to an offence if the person has been given a financial penalty under the regulations in respect of that conduct.
@ref s 1132A(5)(a) The regulations must bar a financial penalty where proceedings are ongoing or the person has been convicted (src:16179-16183)
GIVEN `proceedings have been brought against the person for that offence in respect of that conduct and the proceedings are ongoing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been convicted of that offence in respect of that conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1132A(5)(a) the regulations must provide that no financial penalty may be imposed on the person` MEANS
    IF `proceedings have been brought against the person for that offence in respect of that conduct and the proceedings are ongoing` OR `the person has been convicted of that offence in respect of that conduct`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no financial penalty may be imposed under the regulations on a person in respect of conduct amounting to an offence if— (i) proceedings have been brought ... and the proceedings are ongoing, or (ii) the person has been convicted"

-- src:16183 | (b) no proceedings may be brought against a person in respect of conduct amounting to an offence if the person has been given a financial penalty under the regulations in respect of that conduct.
@ref s 1132A(5)(b) The regulations must bar proceedings once a financial penalty has been given (src:16183)
GIVEN `the person has been given a financial penalty under the regulations in respect of that conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1132A(5)(b) the regulations must provide that no proceedings may be brought against the person` MEANS
    IF `the person has been given a financial penalty under the regulations in respect of that conduct`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no proceedings may be brought against a person in respect of conduct amounting to an offence if the person has been given a financial penalty under the regulations in respect of that conduct"

-- src:16186 | (8) In this section “conduct” means an act or omission.
@ref s 1132A(8) "conduct" (src:16186)
GIVEN `the thing is an act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1132A(8) the thing is conduct` MEANS
    IF `the thing is an act or omission`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “conduct” means an act or omission"

-- ---- s 1133 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16189 | The provisions of this Part except section 1132 do not apply to offences committed before the commencement of the relevant provision.
@ref s 1133 Transitional provision (src:16189)
GIVEN `the provision is section 1132` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence was committed before the commencement of the relevant provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1133 the provision of Part 36 applies to the offence` MEANS
    IF `the provision is section 1132`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of this Part except section 1132"; section 1132 is outside the sentence and the text says nothing else of it
    ELSE IF `the offence was committed before the commencement of the relevant provision`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provisions of this Part except section 1132 do not apply to offences committed before the commencement of the relevant provision"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section says when the provisions do not apply and does not say when they do
